{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-recursive-atom-knot-atlas","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:recursive-atom-knot-atlas","kind":"proposition","title":"Recursive atom-knot atlas at $q_0$ — particles to atoms via Markov-NF braids and hyperbolic-knot closures","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-confined-particle","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-fermion-boson-knot-link","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-confinement-sdp","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp"],"cites":["references/wenzl1988"],"tags":["atlas","recursive","atom-knot","particle-registry","q0","braid-word","markov-closure","hyperbolic-knot","appendix"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.atomKnotAtlas","text":"recursive-atom-knot-atlas.md","leanSource":"recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:recursive-atom-knot-atlas\"></a><p><strong>Atlas (recursive, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code>-indexed).</strong>\n<em>Each confined particle or atom is identified by the Markov-equivalence class of the closure <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\widehat{T_w}</code> of its canonical Hecke element:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">[K]_M \\;=\\; \\bigl[\\,\\widehat{T_w}\\,\\bigr], \\qquad T_w \\in H_{n_0}(q_0), \\quad w \\in B_{n_0},</code></pre>\n<p><em>with confinement at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code> certified by the <a href=\"#prop:confinement-sdp\" data-at=\"mass-theory/hoefsmit-convergence-construction\">confinement SDP</a> and each entry fixed by the <a href=\"#def:confined-particle\" data-at=\"knots-particles-confinement/confined-particles-shells\">confinement source of truth</a>. The registry is recursive: composite entries are assembled from nucleon and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha</code>-cluster constituents, giving uniform comparison against the AME 2020 reference.</em></p>\n<p>The methodology classification, notation legend, braid-closure gallery, the per-level atlas (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell = 0</code> leptons/quarks through <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell = 2</code> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha</code>-cluster atoms), and the per-element AME 2020 cross-reference (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Z = 1</code> to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">118</code>) are recorded in the <a href=\"#rem:recursive-atom-knot-atlas-registry\" data-at=\"appendix-knot-periodic-table/knot-periodic-table\">atlas registry</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"25.3.2","page":"b/prop-recursive-atom-knot-atlas","qa":{"counts":{"pass":84,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":65},"milnor":{"total":1,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.atomKnotAtlas","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
